6182e17f96","position":{"commit_sha":"ff378a7f2199c0c72ca036735bfd6a222050fd08","position":"1786076553221433001-ce81abd2-2d79-4162-acdc-5a6182e17f96"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-223_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6ff494b3-b67f-4284-9d1e-818a0b7eecfd","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented. Gerrit change 1459 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1459), commit b9a65d537d.\n\nTDD evidence: oracle authored RED-first in tests/interfaces/queries/test_terminal_blocker_parity_e63c.py. Behavioral RED reproduced the reported split verbatim -- 'ready and next-batch disagree: ready=False batch=True' -- plus the archived case; a live-blocker negative control passed before and after.\n\nFix: rebar.types.TERMINAL_STATUSES = {closed, archived, deleted} + is_terminal_status(), imported by all four sites (graph/_ready.py, graph/_unblock.py, graph/_graph.py, _engine_support/next_batch.py). Phantom done/completed removed. _ready.py docstring now matches the implemented rule.\n\nTeeth-check (mutation): narrowing the set to {closed} kills 7 tests; re-adding the phantoms kills 4; forcing the predicate True kills 7 (the negative control catches over-widening). Restored: 16/16 green.\nRefactoring litmus: tests assert observable answers and cross-surface agreement only -- no module structure or call-site wiring is pinned.\n\nPre-flight: make lint clean, make typecheck clean (438 files), 648 tests green across tests/interfaces/queries + tests/scripts/graph + lifecycle + delete-unlink.","timestamp":1786069404457871001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 1459 ps2: LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (both gates green) after the generated-types drift fix. Awaiting land.","timestamp":1786073296345464001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSE BLOCKED by the completion verifier on a VALID finding: I updated the module-level docstring in graph/_ready.py but NOT the function-level docstring on find_ready_tickets (~line 47), which still reads 'closed (or tombstoned / missing)' and does not mention archived/deleted. The AC says '_ready.py docstring matches the implemented rule' -- that is not yet fully true. Gerrit 1459 is already MERGED, so this needs a follow-up change; ticket stays in_progress until then. The verifier was right and I am not force-closing past it.","timestamp":1786076553221433001}],"created_at":1786047006622624001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b48f6153-c26e-477a-bca7-dc326ed0c9ae","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1457-9cb2-579a-4607"},{"link_uuid":"7e074264-0322-47ad-ad3d-722e23197c2f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59b1-b706-90e6-489b"},{"link_uuid":"fed10a29-91da-4011-9444-81a28e4f801a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"77de-fb81-3339-4f2d"}],"description":"Four independent definitions of \"this blocker no longer blocks\", with three different memberships:\n\n- `graph/_ready.py:26` `{\"closed\"}`\n- `graph/_unblock.py:26` `{\"closed\", \"deleted\"}`\n- `graph/_graph.py:107` `(\"closed\", \"deleted\")`\n- `_engine_support/next_batch.py:30` `{\"closed\", \"done\", \"completed\", \"deleted\"}`\n\n`done` and `completed` are NOT in the status vocabulary (`types.py:21`,\n`schemas/common.schema.json:9`) — unreachable branches.\n\nReproduced empirically in a throwaway store: with a ticket blocked by a `deleted` ticket,\n`next-batch` offered it while `ready` withheld it. The ordinary path is safe because `delete`\nunlinks peers; only \"link to an already-deleted ticket\" triggers the split.\n\nScope clarified during approval. `ready` and `next-batch` answer DIFFERENT questions by design —\n`ready` has zero file-impact logic; `next-batch` adds conflict-aware batching keyed solely off\ndeclared `file_impact`. That difference is correct and documented. This ticket does NOT merge the\ntwo commands; it unifies the one predicate they both depend on.\n\nMaintainer decision: the terminal set is `{closed, archived, deleted}` — each represents a terminal\nstate. This CHANGES behaviour in three places: `ready` gains `archived` and `deleted`;\n`_unblock`/`_graph` gain `archived`; `next_batch` gains `archived` and loses the phantom values.\n\nNote `_ready.py`'s docstring already says a blocker must be \"closed (or tombstoned / missing)\",\nwhich reads as though `deleted` should count — the code and its own docstring already disagree.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] One shared terminal-state predicate, imported by all four sites\n- [x] The phantom `done`/`completed` values are removed\n- [x] A test asserts `ready` and `next-batch` agree on a ticket blocked by a deleted ticket\n- [x] A test asserts the terminal set is a subset of the schema's status enum, so vocabulary drift fails fast\n- [x] The `_ready.py` docstring matches the implemented rule","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181"],["relates_to","1457-9cb2-579a-4607"],["relates_to","59b1-b706-90e6-489b"],["relates_to","77de-fb81-3339-4f2d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","parent_status_uuid":"889d788b-c90d-4499-a12e-6169169bcdde","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor"],"ticket_id":"e63c-d987-6b99-4b56","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Unify the terminal-state blocker predicate","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["43ec8703-68b6-4aea-9a71-25f5b2d6e398","889d788b-c90d-4499-a12e-6169169bcdde","22fcb013-d4d4-444d-b78f-8d4a5da2e9cc","b94a0e7e-7fa4-4068-9375-e4d216a9f5f4","b48f6153-c26e-477a-bca7-dc326ed0c9ae","7e074264-0322-47ad-ad3d-722e23197c2f","9a9c3fe1-ba39-42ab-b637-3f268b201a83","ccacb109-f88f-4a57-949f-d553656121dc","ce81abd2-2d79-4162-acdc-5a6182e17f96","fed10a29-91da-4011-9444-81a28e4f801a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786078470756534097,"uuid":"9a79ec53-bda5-4715-a58b-3a671e6723de"}